    <defName>RM_Shokka</defName>
    <label>shokka</label>
    <description>Every runway has to surface somewhere - a fog-shadow behind a shrub, a farm's pale wake, ground too dry to grow cover - and the shokka owns those crossings the way a ferryman owns a river. It lies flat in the last of the fuzz with its dappled pelt matching the barrens beyond, and it does nothing at all, sometimes for a day, until something small commits to the open. Locals butcher one warily and waste nothing: the pelt takes dye badly and light beautifully, and a coat of it is the closest a person gets to being hard to see out here.</description>
